Fix verified. Final report:

## Root cause

`Interval.fromISO` (src/interval.js) probes each half of the `/`-separated string with `DateTime.fromISO` to decide whether it is a date or a duration:

```js
const start = DateTime.fromISO(s, opts), end = DateTime.fromISO(e, opts);
if (start.isValid && end.isValid) { ... }
```

`DateTime.fromISO` on a duration string (e.g. `"PT5H30M"`) is unparsable, and with `Settings.throwOnInvalid = true` `DateTime.invalid()` (src/datetime.js:853-864) **throws `InvalidDateTimeError` instead of returning an invalid instance** (same for `Duration.invalid`, src/duration.js:275). So the probe itself blew up before `fromISO` could fall through to the `Duration.fromISO` branch — for both `date/duration` and `duration/date`. With the default setting the probe merely returned an invalid DateTime, which is why the default path worked.

## Change (only file touched: `/luxon/src/interval.js`, `fromISO`, lines 134-170)

Wrapped each `DateTime.fromISO` probe in `try/catch` so a throwing probe is treated as "not a date" and the code falls through to the duration branch (this is exactly upstream Luxon's fix). Also fixed the pre-existing typo in the invalid explanation (`asISO 8601` → `as ISO 8601`; no test asserts it).

```diff
@@ -134,26 +134,39 @@ export default class Interval {
   static fromISO(text, opts) {
     const [s, e] = (text || "").split("/", 2);
     if (s && e) {
-      const start = DateTime.fromISO(s, opts),
+      let start, startIsValid;
+      try {
+        start = DateTime.fromISO(s, opts);
+        startIsValid = start.isValid;
+      } catch (e) {
+        startIsValid = false;
+      }
+
+      let end, endIsValid;
+      try {
         end = DateTime.fromISO(e, opts);
+        endIsValid = end.isValid;
+      } catch (e) {
+        endIsValid = false;
+      }

-      if (start.isValid && end.isValid) {
+      if (startIsValid && endIsValid) {
         return Interval.fromDateTimes(start, end);
       }

-      if (start.isValid) {
+      if (startIsValid) {
         const dur = Duration.fromISO(e, opts);
         if (dur.isValid) {
           return Interval.after(start, dur);
         }
-      } else if (end.isValid) {
+      } else if (endIsValid) {
         const dur = Duration.fromISO(s, opts);
         if (dur.isValid) {
           return Interval.before(end, dur);
         }
       }
     }
-    return Interval.invalid("unparsable", `the input "${text}" can't be parsed asISO 8601`);
+    return Interval.invalid("unparsable", `the input "${text}" can't be parsed as ISO 8601`);
   }
```

