Baseline (before change), `cd /luxon && npx jest test/interval test/datetime test/duration`:
`Test Suites: 1 failed, 44 passed, 45 total; Tests: 2 failed, 794 passed, 796 total` — both failures are pre-existing and unrelated: `test/datetime/toFormat.test.js` French locale hour formatting (`"25 mai 1982 à 9:23:54"` vs expected `"09:23:54"`, ICU/CLDR version issue).

After fix, same command: identical `2 failed, 794 passed` (only the same toFormat failures). Full suite `npx jest`: baseline `2 failed, 892 passed / 894` → after fix `2 failed, 892 passed / 894`. No pre-existing passing test regressed. `npx eslint --quiet src/interval.js` exits 0; `npx prettier --list-different src/interval.js` reports no diff.

Behavioural script (babel-node, run from /luxon so `.babelrc` applies; script deleted afterwards):
```js
Settings.throwOnInvalid = true;
Interval.fromISO("2020-06-22T17:30:00.000+02:00/PT5H30M").toISO()
Interval.fromISO("PT5H30M/2020-06-22T17:30:00.000+02:00").toISO()
```
Result: no throw; both return the same ISO intervals as with the default `throwOnInvalid` (`2020-06-22T11:30:00.000-04:00/2020-06-22T17:00:00.000-04:00` and `2020-06-22T06:00:00.000-04:00/2020-06-22T11:30:00.000-04:00`); also verified identical results for 7 combinations including `{zone:"utc"}` / `{zone:"Europe/Paris"}` opts and date/date intervals ("all identical to default: true"). Genuinely unparsable inputs still throw `InvalidIntervalError` under `throwOnInvalid` (`null`, `""`, `"hello"`, `"foo/bar"`), and `DateTime.fromISO("hello")`/`Duration.fromISO("hello")` still throw their own errors.

Note: `src/impl/util.js` shows as modified in `git status`, but that change was already present in the working tree before I started (I never edited it; it is a pre-existing uncommitted leap-year fix in `objToLocalTS`) and I left it untouched. No test files were modified.

