./docs/zones.md:231:Some local times simply don't exist. The Spring Forward DST shift involves shifting the local time forward by (usually) one hour. In my zone, `America/New_York`, on March 12, 2017 the millisecond after 1:59:59.999 is 3:00:00.000. Thus the times between 2:00:00.000 and 2:59:59.000, inclusive, don't exist in that zone. But of course, nothing stops a user from constructing a DateTime out of that local time.
